hadiths[11]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28186","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: My father married me during the rule of Uthman, and he invited a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Safwan ibn Umayyah came, an old great sheikh, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bite meat with the front teeth, for it is more wholesome and more digestible, or more appetizing and more digestible. Sufyan said: The doubt is from me or from him."
"28187","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: al-Taymi meaning Sulayman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Uthman meaning al-Nahdi, on the authority of Amir ibn Malik, on the authority of Safwan ibn Umayyah, he said: Plague and belly and drowning and childbirth are martyrdom. He said: Abu Uthman narrated it to us many times, and he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once."
"28188","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, on the authority of Umayyah ibn Safwan ibn Umayyah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed from him on the day of Hunayn coats of mail, and he said: Seizure, O Muhammad? He said: Rather a guaranteed loan. He said: Some of it was lost, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered him to guarantee it for him. He said: I today, O Messenger of Allah, am more desirous in Islam."
"28189","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, on the authority of Safwan ibn Abdillah, that Safwan ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf, it was said to him: Perished who did not migrate. He said: I said: I will not reach my family until I come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I rode my mount and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, they claim perished who did not migrate. He said: No, O Abu Wahb, return to the valleys of Makkah. He said: While I was sleeping, the thief came and took my garment from under my head, and I caught him and brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This stole my garment, and he ordered it to be cut. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is not what I wanted, it is upon him as charity. He said: Why not before you brought him to me."
"28190","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Mubarak informed us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Said ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Safwan ibn Umayyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me on the day of Hunayn, and he was the most hateful of people to me, and he kept giving me until he became the most beloved of people to me."
"28191","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said meaning Ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Tariq ibn Muraqqa, on the authority of Safwan ibn Umayyah, that a man stole his cloak and he raised him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered its cutting. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have pardoned him. He said: Why was this not before you brought him to me, O Abu Wahb? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut him."
"28192","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Tawus narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Safwan ibn Umayyah, that it was said to him: None enters Paradise except who migrated. He said: I said: I will not enter my house until I come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this stole a garment of mine for a man with him, and he ordered its cutting. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have gifted it to him. He said: Why not before you brought him to me. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, they say none enters Paradise except who migrated. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No migration after the conquest of Makkah, but jihad and intention, and when you are called to march, march."
"28193","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Uthman meaning al-Nahdi, on the authority of Amir ibn Malik, on the authority of Safwan ibn Umayyah, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Plague is martyrdom, and drowning is martyrdom, and belly is martyrdom, and childbirth is martyrdom."
"28194","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Amir ibn Malik, on the authority of Safwan ibn Umayyah, he said: Plague and belly and drowning and childbirth are martyrdom. Sulayman said: He narrated it to us, meaning Abu Uthman, many times, and raised it once to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"28195","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah, on the authority of Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, he said: Safwan ibn Umayyah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me while I take meat from the bone with my hand, and he said: O Safwan. I said: At your service. He said: Bring meat near to your mouth, for it is more wholesome and more digestible."
"28196","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman meaning Ibn Qarm narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Humayd, son of the sister of Safwan ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Safwan ibn Umayyah, he said: I was sleeping in the mosque upon a garment of mine and it was stolen, and we seized the thief and raised him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered its cutting. I said: O Messenger of Allah, for a garment of mine worth thirty dirhams, I gift it to him or sell it to him. He said: Why was it not before you brought him to me."
